{"tool_name":"epina-image-lab","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><em>Epina ImageLab</em><span> is a Microsoft Windows-based multisensor imaging tool for processing and analyzing hyperspectral images. It is a modular system consisting of a basic engine, a graphical user interface, a chemometrics toolbox and optional user-supplied modules. It supports the most important spectroscopic imaging techniques, such as UV/Vis, infrared, Raman, THz, optical emission/absorption, and mass spectrometry. On top of that </span><em>Epina ImageLab</em><span> enables the user to merge hyperspectral images with maps of physical properties and conventional high-resolution color photos.&nbsp;</span></p>","summary":"","value":"<p><em>Epina ImageLab</em><span> is a Microsoft Windows-based multisensor imaging tool for processing and analyzing hyperspectral images. It is a modular system consisting of a basic engine, a graphical user interface, a chemometrics toolbox and optional user-supplied modules. It supports the most important spectroscopic imaging techniques, such as UV/Vis, infrared, Raman, THz, optical emission/absorption, and mass spectrometry. On top of that </span><em>Epina ImageLab</em><span> enables the user to merge hyperspectral images with maps of physical properties and conventional high-resolution color photos.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-05-17T17:57:56+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-11-22T05:09:27+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[{"cid":null,"comment_count":null,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":null,"last_comment_uid":null,"status":2}],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1574399563,"last_comment_uid":1,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"ImageLab"}],"has_biological_t